<title>JAPAN: Mitsubishi Chemical says to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Mitsubishi Chemical says to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Japanese chemical company Mitsubishi Chemical Corp announced on Monday that it plans to buy back up to 40 billion yen worth of its own stock, or up to 100 million shares.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it would seek approval of the share buy-back plan at a shareholders' meeting to be held on June 27.  </p>
<p>Mitsubishi Chemical said it would offer to buy back its shares at levels below the actual market price.</p>
<p>Shell Petroleum Co Ltd and Shell Japan Ltd, which hold a combined 118 million shares, or 5.38 percent stake, in Mitsubishi Chemical, have expressed their intention to sell most of their Mitsubishi Chemical shares and are likely to respond to the offer unless the share price falls drastically or the yen weakens further, the company said.</p>
</text>
